     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I understand you've confirmed it, but I can't verify the clinical rationale. No standard indication supports amlodipine 50 mg daily, and that dose is in the range where overdose toxicity is reported. The risks are profound hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and they can last more than 24 hours. The harm would be serious and hard to reverse, so I'm not comfortable entering it as written.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum labeled dose, and titrate from there. I can do this now.\n- **Add another agent** if 10 mg isn't enough. Combining a different antihypertensive class is the usual approach.\n- **Call pharmacy or the attending.** If there's an unusual indication, such as a specialist-directed protocol, they can review it and place or co-sign the order through their own channel.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter 10 mg, or a different dose."
      }
     ],
